if / elif / else: branching
def battery_status(T):
    """Classify battery temperature T in Celsius."""
    if T &gt; 60:
        return "SHUTDOWN"
    elif T &gt; 45:
        return "warning"
    else:
        return "nominal"
Reading rule: conditions are checked top to bottom, and only the first true branch runs. Trace battery_status(50): is 50 &gt; 60? No. Is 50 &gt; 45? Yes → "warning", done — the else never even gets looked at. Now predict battery_status(60) — exactly 60. (Not greater than 60, so not shutdown: "warning". Is that what a battery engineer wants at exactly the shutdown threshold? That’s not a Python question. Hold that thought.)
